; ============================================================================
; SCRATCH IS NOT A TABLE -- AIF-133
; ============================================================================
;
; WHAT MAKES THIS A DISCRIMINATOR AND NOT A DEMONSTRATION.
;
; SSC_T1 is the arm. It asks ONE question -- is the table in AREA 0 the REAL
; one -- and that question has different answers on the two builds:
;
;     before AIF-133   Area 0: SSTAB.__fldbak.dbf     T1 reads .F.
;     after  AIF-133   Area 0: SSTAB.dbf              T1 reads .T.
;
; A FIELDMGR restructure leaves <stem>.__fldbak.dbf beside the real table and
; the directory scan tested the EXTENSION only, so the backup was opened as a
; work area. The scan also SORTS BY FILENAME, and ".__fldbak" sorts before
; ".dbf" -- so the backup did not tag along at the end, it TOOK AREA 0 and
; shifted every area after it. A posture saved from that state records a backup
; as the active table; a MINIDB save carries its bytes; WRITEBACK returns them
; to disk. Measured 2026-08-26: STUDENTS.__fldbak.dbf was a 22,425-byte member
; of a live container.
;
; WHY THE ARM IS PHRASED POSITIVELY.
;
; The defect is "an extra table was opened", so the tempting arm is "the scratch
; table is ABSENT". NO MARKER IN THIS LANGUAGE CAN ASSERT ABSENCE -- USE_AGAIN
; established that over three cuts, and an ERRORED marker PRINTS NOTHING rather
; than going red, so a suite can lose the claim and still report a full green.
; This spec asks the answerable question instead: DID THE REAL TABLE LAND IN
; AREA 0. That is true only when the scratch was skipped, and it is a field
; comparison rather than a console read -- per the doctrine FIELDMGR_APPEND paid
; for, a spec that asserts SHAPE passes green on a blanked table.
;
; The two fixtures carry DIFFERENT marks for exactly this reason. If both said
; "REAL" the arm would pass on either build and prove nothing.
;
; GUARDS. If either SSC_G* reds, treat SSC_T1 as UNPROVEN rather than as
; passing. G0 proves the real table carries REAL; G1 proves the backup EXISTS
; and carries BACK. Without G1 an arm reading "REAL" cannot tell "the scratch
; was correctly skipped" from "the scratch was never created" -- and the second
; is a fixture failure wearing a fix's clothes, which is the WSL_G4/G5 lesson:
; guard every input an arm reads, not just the interesting ones.
;
; ISOLATED BY CONSTRUCTION. This spec opens a DIRECTORY, so a stray table left
; by another spec would join the scan and could take area 0 on its own. It
; therefore creates its own directory under SANDBOX and scans only that --
; CREATE makes the path when it does not exist. Nothing here depends on what
; the shared sandbox happens to contain.
;
; TEARDOWN SPELLS OUT ".dbf", AND THAT IS THE SAME DEFECT ONE DOOR ALONG.
; `ERASE SSTAB.__fldbak CONFIRM` answers "Table not found" while the file is
; sitting there: the table-token form appends .dbf only when it does not already
; see an extension, and ".__fldbak" looks like one. So ERASE cannot address a
; name whose second segment resembles an extension -- the same root cause as the
; scan defect this spec covers, in a different verb. Naming the file in full is
; the way through, and it is written out here rather than quietly worked around.
;
; Self-bootstrapping SSTAB / SSTAB.__fldbak in SANDBOX/SSC, erased at both ends
; so a re-run cannot read the previous run's fixture. Leaves an empty directory.
; ============================================================================

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/SSC

; Prior-run residue. A refusal here is noise, not a failure.
ERASE SSTAB CONFIRM
ERASE SSTAB.__fldbak.dbf CONFIRM

; The backup is made from the table BEFORE the table is edited, which is what a
; restructure backup actually is: an older copy of the same file.
CREATE X64 SSTAB (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "BACK"
COPY TO SSTAB.__fldbak OVERWRITE
CLOSE

USE SSTAB
REPLACE MARK WITH "REAL"
? "SSC_G0_real_table_carries_REAL:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "REAL")
CLOSE

USE SSTAB.__fldbak
? "SSC_G1_backup_exists_and_carries_BACK:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BACK")
CLOSE

; --- THE ARM ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Scan the directory. Area 0 must be the real table.

WORKSPACE OPEN DBF
SELECT 0
? "SSC_T1_area0_is_the_real_table:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "REAL")

WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL

ERASE SSTAB CONFIRM
ERASE SSTAB.__fldbak.dbf CONFIRM
